  updates  >  Mneme updates family — 1 action(s). Run \`mneme updates --help\` for actions, or \`mneme updates <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  handoff  >  Mneme handoff family — 5 action(s). Run \`mneme handoff --help\` for actions, or \`mneme handoff <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  birthright  >  Mneme birthright family — 2 action(s). Run \`mneme birthright --help\` for actions, or \`mneme birthright <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  clone  >  Mneme clone family — 1 action(s). Run \`mneme clone --help\` for actions, or \`mneme clone <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  beacon  >  Mneme beacon family — 2 action(s). Run \`mneme beacon --help\` for actions, or \`mneme beacon <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  stargate  >  Mneme stargate family — 1 action(s). Run \`mneme stargate --help\` for actions, or \`mneme stargate <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  cosmic  >  Mneme cosmic family — 7 action(s). Run \`mneme cosmic --help\` for actions, or \`mneme cosmic <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  bounty  >  Mneme bounty family — 3 action(s). Run \`mneme bounty --help\` for actions, or \`mneme bounty <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  replica  >  Mneme replica family — 2 action(s). Run \`mneme replica --help\` for actions, or \`mneme replica <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  infra  >  Mneme infra family — 3 action(s). Run \`mneme infra --help\` for actions, or \`mneme infra <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  genesis  >  Mneme genesis family — 3 action(s). Run \`mneme genesis --help\` for actions, or \`mneme genesis <action> --json '{...}'\` to invoke.
  help [command]  >  display help for command

Advanced commands (Phase 2/3/4 + WILD ideas) are hidden from this help.
Run \`mneme advanced\` to see them.

"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme advanced\` snapshot 1`] = `
"
  μνήμη  >  ·  Mneme — advanced commands
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Phase 2 — semantic similarity
    entities  >  parse + embed every TS/JS/Python/Go symbol
    clones [--threshold]  >  surface near-duplicate functions

  Phase 3 — incident correlation
    correlate --source ...  >  join commits with incidents (pager / manual)
    blast <commit>  >  predict incidents likely to follow a commit
    palimpsest <file>:<line>  >  walk the causal chain of a single line
    conscience [files...]  >  risk-score a PR against history

  Wisdom Mutant Engine (Phase 4)
    feedback <id> up|down  >  record explicit feedback on a query
    calibrate  >  re-tune search knobs against feedback set

  Insights — the killer commands
    who-knows <topic>  >  verdict on who knows X (% confidence + backup + risk)
    decisions  >  auto-extract ADRs from commit messages
    stack-trace [--from F]  >  paste an error, get historical context per frame
    story <topic>  >  narrate the evolution of <topic> across acts
    dream  >  speculative ideas grounded in your patterns
    chat  >  multi-turn REPL over your repo's history

  Innovations (Sprint 4) — wisdom + world-class + uniqueness
    regret  >  commits shipped + immediately fixed/reverted (regret rate)
    bus-factor  >  files where one author owns ≥75% — fragility map
    paradox  >  architectural flip-flops (A → B → A patterns)
    commit-coach [--stdin]  >  pre-commit review: message + reviewers + warnings
    crystal-ball [--stdin]  >  predict CI/follow-up failure probability for staged diff

  Quant (Sprint 5) — Wall Street meets Git
    drawdown  >  worst losing streaks (firefighting periods)
    alpha --items F  >  Kelly-criterion allocation for technical debt
    backtest --samples F  >  validate any predictor against history
    black-swan  >  rare-but-catastrophic file patterns
    insider-trading  >  authors who fix bugs they introduced
    moneyball  >  undervalued contributors (high ROI, low LOC)
    greek  >  codebase Greeks (Δ Γ Θ) sensitivity
    correlation-matrix  >  hidden behavioral coupling between files
    implied-volatility  >  chaos predicted from commit message tone
    tax-loss-harvest  >  dead-code deletion candidates

  WILD — opinionated extras
    heal [--dry-run]  >  synthesize WHY notes for poor commit messages
    echo [--id|--query]  >  find past incidents resembling current
    runaway  >  files growing silently across many commits
    mirror  >  onboarding dossier (5 PRs, 3 people, 2 incidents)
    rumor  >  tribal phrases mentioned but never documented
    fossil  >  files deleted from HEAD but alive in history
    ledger --since ...  >  tamper-evident audit log (SOX/SOC2)
    adapt  >  mutant detector — recommend next 1-3 commands
    teach <target>  >  explain a folder/file in plain language
    genius <question>  >  multi-step LLM agent over Mneme commands

  Brand
    wisdom [-n <1..13>]  >  a meditation from the Mneme manifesto
    manifesto  >  the full canon

  Each command has its own --help with options and examples.
  Full design notes: WILD_IDEAS.md, ROADMAP.md.
"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme ask --help\` snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: mneme ask [options] <question...>

Ask the memory: "why does payment.ts use try/catch?"

Options:
  -k, --top-k <n>  >  number of results (default: 8)
  --json  >  machine-readable JSON output (default: false)
  --no-llm  >  skip LLM synthesis — extractive answer only
  --debug  >  show intent classification + raw scores (default:
                         false)
  --audit  >  refuse to answer below confidence floor or with
                         unverified citations (default: false)
  --audit-floor <level>  >  audit confidence floor: low | medium | high (default:
                         "medium")
  --stream  >  v0.23: emit speculative-reasoning events in real-time
                         (consider/accept/prune/verify) (default: false)
  -h, --help  >  display help for command
"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme do --help\` snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: mneme do [options] <query...>

Smart dispatcher — describe what you want, Mneme picks tools and runs them ('do
find security issues' / 'do is the codebase healthy')

Options:
  --json  >  structured output (default: false)
  -h, --help  >  display help for command
"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme forensics anomaly --help\` snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: mneme forensics anomaly [options]

Catch suspicious commits before merge (insider-threat / credential-compromise)

Options:
  --threshold <n>  >  deviation threshold to surface (0..4) (default: 0.9)
  --top <n>  >  show N findings (default: 10)
  --json  >  structured output (default: false)
  -h, --help  >  display help for command
"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme guardian --help\` snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: mneme guardian [options]

24/7 self-healing engine — diagnose weaknesses + auto-fix safe actions

Options:
  --watch  >  run forever, polling every --interval seconds (default:
                        false)
  --once  >  run a single pass and exit (default if --watch is
                        absent) (default: false)
  --interval <seconds>  >  poll interval in seconds (--watch only) (default: 300)
  --apply  >  actually apply auto-policy actions (otherwise
                        observe-only) (default: false)
  --max-iterations <n>  >  stop after N ticks (testing / cron-style)
  --json  >  structured JSON output (default: false)
  -h, --help  >  display help for command
"
`;

exports[`CLI regression — output structure snapshots > \`mneme htc-stats --help\` snapshot 1`] = `
"Usage: mneme htc-stats [options]

Inspect HTC coverage + compression ratio (raw vs cached tokens)

Options:
  --json  >  machine-readable output (default: false)
  -h, --help  >  display help for command
"
`;

